  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">INTEGRATED MANAGEMENT &amp; ENHANCEMENT OF C</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is the second phase of managing three inland lagoons (Bustillos, Santiaguillo and Babicora) that are used by waterfowl to migrate across the Chihuahuan Desert. The project will protect 7,659.47 acres through conservation agreements. It will enhance 807.69 acres to diminish water runoff, improve grasslands and increase water catchment, and develop management plans for 6,382.48 acres. It will also build and install domestic water sanitation systems, and develop a participatory business plan for the sustainable management and conservation of Babicora Lagoon. It will strengthen decision-making processes using remote sensing to classify erosion, land-use and hydrological changes in the three watersheds, track territorial planning, and coordinate overwintering bird monitoring in the three lagoons.</narrative>
  </description>
